From 9c7e5a1d3f2b4c6d8e0f1a2b3c4d5e6f708192a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: m5agent <m5agent@m5stack.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 01:35:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hw/m5stopwatch: add Unit batch-7 remaining seven data planes

Implement the remaining batch-7 Unit contracts on top of the 25-layer
reconciled canonical chain (through 0144). No guest/Device Service evidence is
recorded; all seven stay planned and the reused models keep their existing
NOT RUN boundaries.

- hex (A045): alias of the existing 37-LED RMT capture branch used by neohex;
  public UIFlow2 has no unit/hex.py so the generic neopixel driver is the only
  reference. SK6812 vs WS2812C timing/order stays UNRESOLVED, and PORT.B yellow
  data conflicts with neohex/rgb-led-10cm/op90.
- mini-pdm (U089): DEFERRED, no QEMU Unit model. Public source has no Unit
  driver and the existing SPM1423 PDM RX path is board-level I2S, not an
  attachment the Unit runtime can bind. The catalog/profile entry documents the
  driver-gap and acoustic boundary; no fake PCM fixture is added.
- catm (U128), catm-gnss (U137), lorawan-cn470 (U184-CN470): extend the shared
  UART fixture responder (guest TX capture + idle-time response injection) by
  unit id only. No AT decoding/protocol claim is made: SIM7080G AT/URC order,
  cellular + GNSS concurrency and GNSS COG semantics stay UNRESOLVED; the
  LoRaWAN product is STM32WLE5/RAK3172 while the frozen driver is ASR650x.
- can (U085) and mini-can (U179): bind a real CanBusClient to the cores3
  m5-canbus created by the board. Guest TWAI frames are observed
  (frames-observed/last-frame-hex) and a QOM inject-hex fixture sends one frame
  onto the same bus (injected-frames). Frame direction/filtering/bit timing,
  external transceiver/isolation/termination and bus arbitration are NOT
  modeled. QOM smoke on S3 uses M5SW_CAN_ECHO to validate the loop path.
- mini-imu-pro (U171): new US_BMI270 primary at 0x68 plus the existing BMP280
  secondary at 0x76 on one Grove pair. BMI270 accepts the CMD 0x7E init burst
  and exposes synthetic accel/gyro/temperature registers; BMM150 is a
  simplified 16-bit window at 0x04..0x09 (raw=uT*16). The full BMI270 init blob
  execution, aux transaction semantics, range configuration, real motion and
  magnetic/attitude physics are NOT modeled; 0x68 conflicts with mini-imu U095
  and 0x76 with env/bps/env-ii/env-iv.

Offline QOM smoke (S3 m5cores3, no guest firmware) attaches hex, catm,
catm-gnss, lorawan-cn470, can, mini-can and mini-imu-pro and validates property
registration, responder fixtures, CAN injection/observation and the
BMI270+BMP280 dual attach: 7/7 attach and property checks PASS. The smoke does
NOT cover guest byte semantics, LED timing, AT decode, CAN bit timing or IMU
physics.
